# Testing Guidelines

## Component Testing

- Use @testing-library/react for component tests
- Test user interactions, not implementation details
- Use MSW for API mocking in tests
- Test component rendering and behavior
- Test error states and loading states

## Test File Naming

- `component-name.test.tsx` for component tests
- `hook-name.test.ts` for hook tests
- `utility-name.test.ts` for utility tests
- `api-name.test.ts` for API tests

## Testing Patterns

- Test component rendering
- Test user interactions (clicks, form submissions)
- Test error states
- Test loading states
- Mock external dependencies
- Test accessibility features

## MSW Setup

- Create handlers for API endpoints
- Use realistic response data
- Test error scenarios
- Mock different response states

## Test Structure

```typescript
import { render, screen, fireEvent, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { rest } from 'msw';
import { setupServer } from 'msw/node';
import { EventCard } from './event-card';

const server = setupServer(
  rest.get('/api/events', (req, res, ctx) => {
    return res(ctx.json([
      { id: '1', title: 'Test Event', content: 'Test Content' }
    ]));
  })
);

beforeAll(() => server.listen());
afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers());
afterAll(() => server.close());

describe('EventCard', () => {
  it('should render event data correctly', () => {
    const event = {
      id: '1',
      title: 'Test Event',
      content: 'Test Content',
      createdAt: new Date()
    };

    render(<EventCard event={event} onEdit={jest.fn()} onDelete={jest.fn()} />);

    expect(screen.getByText('Test Event')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByText('Test Content')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('should call onEdit when edit button is clicked', () => {
    const onEdit = jest.fn();
    const event = { id: '1', title: 'Test', content: 'Test' };

    render(<EventCard event={event} onEdit={onEdit} onDelete={jest.fn()} />);

    fireEvent.click(screen.getByText('Edit'));
    expect(onEdit).toHaveBeenCalledWith('1');
  });

  it('should show loading state', () => {
    render(<EventCard event={null} onEdit={jest.fn()} onDelete={jest.fn()} isLoading={true} />);

    expect(screen.getByTestId('loading-skeleton')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

## Hook Testing

```typescript
import { renderHook, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { useEvents } from './use-events';

describe('useEvents', () => {
  it('should fetch events successfully', async () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useEvents());

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(result.current.isLoading).toBe(false);
    });

    expect(result.current.data).toHaveLength(1);
    expect(result.current.error).toBeNull();
  });

  it('should handle error state', async () => {
    server.use(
      rest.get('/api/events', (req, res, ctx) => {
        return res(ctx.status(500));
      }),
    );

    const { result } = renderHook(() => useEvents());

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(result.current.error).toBeTruthy();
    });
  });
});
```

## Utility Testing

```typescript
import { formatDate, validateEmail } from './utils';

describe('formatDate', () => {
  it('should format date correctly', () => {
    const date = new Date('2023-01-15');
    expect(formatDate(date)).toBe('Jan 15, 2023');
  });

  it('should handle invalid date', () => {
    expect(formatDate(null)).toBe('Invalid date');
  });
});

describe('validateEmail', () => {
  it('should validate correct email', () => {
    expect(validateEmail('test@example.com')).toBe(true);
  });

  it('should reject invalid email', () => {
    expect(validateEmail('invalid-email')).toBe(false);
  });
});
```

## Integration Testing

- Test complete user workflows
- Test form submissions
- Test navigation between pages
- Test data persistence

## E2E Testing (Future)

- Use Playwright or Cypress
- Test critical user paths
- Test responsive design
- Test accessibility features

## Test Coverage

- Aim for 80%+ code coverage
- Focus on business logic
- Test edge cases
- Test error scenarios

## Performance Testing

- Test component rendering performance
- Test bundle size
- Test memory leaks
- Test loading times
